You can connect the camera directly to a printer and print out the images in the CF card. This chapter explains how to print your digital camera photos with a printer capable of direct printing via Bubble Jet Direct standard.

<PIC:Manual10_188>
{{image description: Compatibility chart showing Canon CP printer, Canon BJ printer, and Non-Canon printer categories, with icons for CP Direct, PictBridge, and Bubble Jet Direct and page ranges below.}}

When connecting the cable plug to the camera's <DIGITAL> terminal, the cable plug's the Multi-controller icon must face the front side of the camera. To connect to the printer, refer to the printer's instruction manual.

<PIC:Manual10_192>
{{image description: Line drawing close-up showing a cable connector being inserted into the camera digital port, with a callout magnifying the connector symbol.}}

If you are using a Canon printer, refer to the printer's instruction manual for the recommended paper type settings.

<PIC:Manual10_201>
{{image description: Table mapping paper type names to media: Photo to Photo Paper Plus Glossy, Fast Photo to Photo Paper Pro, and Default to Photo Paper Plus Glossy.}}

Set the print type, date imprinting, and file No. imprinting. The print settings will be applied to all print-ordered images. (They cannot be set individually for each image.)

<PIC:Manual10_223>
